WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:10.600
Hi, I'm Sagar Pandya.

00:10.600 --> 00:12.840
A few years ago, I was running

00:12.840 --> 00:15.880
my IT and cybersecurity consulting company.

00:15.880 --> 00:19.760
Things were stable until suddenly they weren't.

00:19.760 --> 00:23.360
Overnight, every client conversation shifted.

00:23.360 --> 00:27.560
It went from how do we stay secure to,

00:27.560 --> 00:30.280
what are we supposed to do with AI?

00:30.280 --> 00:34.140
Internally, my team was feeling the weight too.

00:34.140 --> 00:36.760
Uncertainty, confusion.

00:36.760 --> 00:38.440
There was no roadmap,

00:38.440 --> 00:40.240
no expert to lean on.

00:40.240 --> 00:42.640
But everyone kept looking at me,

00:42.640 --> 00:44.960
hoping that I had the answers.

00:44.960 --> 00:47.200
That's when I realized something.

00:47.200 --> 00:48.840
I couldn't fake it.

00:48.840 --> 00:53.040
I couldn't lead from a place of control or ego.

00:53.040 --> 00:57.280
I had to shift from knowing to listening.

00:57.280 --> 01:00.240
From managing pressure to moving

01:00.240 --> 01:03.000
through it with my team by my side.

01:03.000 --> 01:06.240
So I stopped trying to lead the conversation,

01:06.240 --> 01:09.800
and instead started creating space for it.

01:09.800 --> 01:12.160
I brought my team together.

01:12.160 --> 01:15.840
We didn't talk tech, we talked mission.

01:15.840 --> 01:18.200
What's all of our role in this?

01:18.200 --> 01:20.000
What do we believe in,

01:20.000 --> 01:22.200
even if things get chaotic?

01:22.200 --> 01:24.840
That was a start of real alignment,

01:25.280 --> 01:29.560
and that clarity gave us permission to try,

01:29.560 --> 01:32.400
to experiment, to ask.

01:32.400 --> 01:34.640
That's when agility showed up.

01:34.640 --> 01:38.120
Not in speed, but in shared momentum.

01:38.120 --> 01:40.240
So here's what I'll tell you.

01:40.240 --> 01:43.680
If you're leading a team through change right now,

01:43.680 --> 01:46.480
you don't need to be the smartest voice in the room.

01:46.480 --> 01:48.640
You need to be the clearest.

01:48.640 --> 01:53.040
Alignment starts with pausing and asking

01:53.040 --> 01:56.000
what matters to us in this moment.

01:56.000 --> 01:59.040
And agility follows when you give your team permission

01:59.040 --> 02:01.640
to grow, not just perform.

02:02.600 --> 02:04.680
So here's your challenge.

02:04.680 --> 02:07.800
This week, take 15 minutes with your team.

02:08.720 --> 02:12.080
Don't talk metrics, but just ask one question.

02:13.120 --> 02:15.920
What's our mission right now in this season?

02:17.080 --> 02:18.240
And then just listen.

02:19.240 --> 02:24.240
Because leadership in flow isn't about moving fast.

02:24.680 --> 02:27.360
It's about getting clear together.

